#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:5
#: 60948b02e42046118ba1cee289cd858a
msgid "Using an External Compass with APM 2.x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:9
#: 6cdb061a818b402ab8f74706767677d2
msgid "**ARCHIVED**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:11
#: b9c97ad1cce148bf951cf9c90477bbec
msgid "The APM2.x is end of life for use with ArduPilot. This article is made available for existing users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:14
#: 6f5c9a75406d4ea085103ff539cce525
msgid "If you're having trouble with magnetic noise affecting your compass onboard the APM 2.5 board, you may want to switch to an external compass that you can mount further away from noise sources such as motors. This article explains how."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:23
#: efaafec3c6a14e82a5d90930b6b9673b
msgid "Step-by-step instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:25
#: 8e817e6130d145c29d52b9c938436623
msgid "Purchase a `HMC5883L magnetometer breakout board <http://store.jdrones.com/APM2_6_Compass_HMC5883_p/jdmagnet001.htm>`__. Make sure the 3DR board is set to use 3.3volts (the APM 2.5’s I2C port uses 3.3 volts, not 5 volts). You will have to modify the 3DR board because it is shipped from 3DR with the 5 volt jumper set, as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:34
#: 6d8798649565450d9f87df0c152a1304
msgid "Looking at the below picture, cut the jumper trace in the middle of the APM 2.5 board. This disables the SDA line to the board’s internal compass, rendering it inert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:41
#: 1ea497a0bbb247339c44ca481840830a
msgid "The APM 2.5 I2C connector needs a 4 pin DF13 connector (like `this one <http://store.jdrones.com/cable_df13_4pin_15cm_p/cbldf13p4c15.htm>`__). Cut off one and and strip and tin the four wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:43
#: 06a098070c334e0f97d8300ad6e46dda
msgid "Connect the DF13’s 4 wires to the compass breakout board. Note that the wires will not be one to one. Pin 1 on the DF13 connector will not go to pin 1 of the compass board. The standard 3DR cable has one red wire and three black wires. Substitute your wire colors accordingly. Solder the wires as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:49
#: 1d3157ec3e52478484eb76407e8252dd
msgid "Red wire on end of connector (+3.3v) goes to the VCC (or +3.3v) pad on the compass board (see labels on board for location). This is the wire closest to the interior on the APM 2.5 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:52
#: 3fb175fb2e7b41d9b0fb40ea5652fbf3
msgid "Wire next to red wire (SCL) goes to the SCL pad on the compass board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:54
#: f59daf276d83424aac2c784f7258b531
msgid "Wire next to wire next to red wire (SDA) goes to the SDA pad on compass board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:56
#: e5cdeae76a77420abce807f720d23c40
msgid "Black wire on end of connector (ground) goes to ground pad on compass board. This is the wire closest to the edge of the APM 2.5 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:60
#: 765599d7439442b4985cc9e975b3a26f
msgid "Mount the compass board on the top plate of your quad. Double-sided foam tape works well for this. The orientation of the board matters. In the picture below, we've mounted the board “components up with pins forward”. Note which direction you mount the board – you will need to modify the software with this orientation, as explained in the next step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:70
#: 59f4d527a14c4d04b910646193f11f74
msgid "Modify, compile and load the software for your compass board orientation. You must be able to load software from the Arduino IDE to complete this step. In “APM_Config.h”, you will find a commented out statement like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:79
#: 85a303bbca59494f954337981e5b507b
msgid "For the orientation shown in the picture above, for example, you would add the following statement just below the commented out statement above as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:88
#: 27437f60eaa44d41ad96994533ed0f90
msgid "You can find a list of all possible orientations for the ``MAG_ORIENTATION`` flag in the **AP_Compass_HMC5843.h** library, including orientations for both the 3DR and Sparkfun boards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:92
#: 54585712d8e745b7aab95aa472be81ea
msgid "If this is the first time loading software from the IDE, make sure the following statement is uncommented:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:99
#: 812803ae2c4b457bba0e6155a4898455
msgid "Save, Compile and Upload the modified software"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/externalmagentometer-apm2x.rst:100
#: b0dfef13a4244f2c92902194c9eab880
msgid "Test the compass board and have fun flying with a now stable compass!"
msgstr ""

